WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:30.080 --> 00:01:05.240
[Music]

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.040
[Narrator:] This motion picture clinic is
the first attempt of its kind to present,

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:16.589
for the use of physicians only, a clinic covering
the diagnosis, treatment, 

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.200
and general care of a disease.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:27.500
We present first Dr. Charles Gordon Heyd of New York City, president of the American Medical Association,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.880
who speaks to you from the headquarters of the Association in Chicago.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:38.880
[Dr. Heyd:] The American Medical Association is delighted to join forces with the

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.120
United States Public Health Service in the endeavor to stamp out syphilis.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:49.000
Other nations have shown us that much can
be done. 

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:54.300
Man has the ability to banish infectious diseases from the earth.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:02:01.300
The purpose of this film is to provide every
doctor with a complete resume 

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:06.660
of the present-day knowledge of syphilis in all of its phases.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:12.430
There comes from the public an insistent demand for medical services in the prevention,

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.760
the diagnosis, and the treatment of this disease.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.760
The time is opportune. The necessity for eradication
is imperative.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:30.190
The American Medical Association offers this
motion picture to the medical profession as

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:37.190
a new type of medical teaching, and as a significant
contribution to graduate medical instruction.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.480
[Narrator:] We move next to the headquarters
of the United States Public Health Service

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:51.279
in Washington DC. Dr. Thomas Parran, Surgeon
General, speaks.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.620
[Dr. Parran:] Our two great medical forces,
the private physicians and the health officers,

00:02:56.629 --> 00:03:00.139
have joined hands in this campaign against
syphilis.

00:03:00.139 --> 00:03:07.139
To the private physician, I would say, diagnose
syphilis early. Treat syphilis adequately.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:14.760
Report your new cases, and your last cases.
Teach syphilis to your individual patients.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:22.139
To the health officer, I would say, learn
the extent of your syphilis problem.

00:03:22.139 --> 00:03:25.799
Provide adequate treatment facilities and a complete laboratory service.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:33.360
Find new cases. Maintain an efficient follow-up
service. And teach syphilis to the masses.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:39.730
By the consistent application of these principles,
this disease can be brought under control.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:45.559
Our children will hold us criminally careless and incompetent if, with the means at hand,

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:49.459
we fail to end this scourge within our generation.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:54.120
Syphilis must be the next great plague to go. We must attack it now.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:01.139
[Narrator:] Dr. John A. Stokes, Professor
of Dermatology and Syphilology in the University

00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:06.499
of Pennsylvania's School of Medicine, presents
the diagnosis of early syphilis.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:11.999
[Dr. Stokes:] The diagnosis of early syphilis, primary and secondary, is a laboratory problem.

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:17.669
The physician in practice must therefore suspect,
examine, closely and completely.

00:04:17.669 --> 00:04:23.060
Collect diagnostic material. Collect it again
and again. If you cannot do so, call an expert

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:29.030
who can. Follow tenaciously and relentlessly,
through time, and with the aid of contact

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:33.660
tracing and serologic follow-up, each case
to a definite conclusion.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.840
The old-time clinical criteria for differentiation
of early syphilis are unsound diagnostically

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.500
in primary syphilis, intricate and puzzling
in secondary syphilis, 

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.700
procrastinating and dangerous in both.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.210
The chancre may occur anywhere except on the teeth and nails.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.960
May be too small to be visible to the patient. So large as to deceive the physician.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:05:00.060
May not develop at all. May be superposed
on any open wound or sore. 

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:05.680
Does not require previous abrasion. May be out of sight in urethra or on cervix.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:11.260
May be masked by the discharge of a gonorrhea or produce its own urethral discharge.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:16.060
Histories of exposure and calculated incubation periods are unreliable.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:23.060
Do not expect to see typical lesions. Regard
all genital lesions with some suspicion.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.740
And in all lesions, genital or extra-genital,
look for but do not overweigh

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.820
the three great suspicion-arousing features of indolence:

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:39.810
induration, firm or cartilaginous feel, satellite adenopathy, a local lymph node enlargement-

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:46.400
bilateral on the genitalia, unilateral elsewhere, discrete, usually not tender.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:52.909
In particular, make no final clinical diagnosis of chancroid, exclusive of syphilis on any

00:05:52.909 --> 00:05:57.419
but serologic follow-up tests. Mixed ulcers
are common.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:03.080
The darkfield examination is critically important
in the first week of the primary lesion,

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:08.200
less so the second week, and merely confirmatory of serologic diagnosis, 

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.340
though usefully so, thereafter.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:15.270
Though an untreated lesion is desirable, it
is not indispensable. 

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:22.080
Salt-solution soaking for 24 hours, aspiration of an indurated base,

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.920
[The physician holds up the various instruments needed to perform these tests.]

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:29.620
suction after vigorous rubbing or scraping,

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.900
aspiration of adjacent lymph nodes.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:39.780
Repeated collection of material on successive days may yield a positive darkfield.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:45.670
The inexperienced physician is not encouraged
to use the darkfield microscope.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:50.080
The direct darkfield examination from the fresh specimen is, however, 

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:54.159
the ideal when performed by the experienced or expert.

00:06:54.939 --> 00:06:59.949
The essential requirements for satisfactory
material intended for darkfield examination

00:06:59.949 --> 00:07:05.669
for Spirochaeta pallida are: lymph or blood
serum, not blood, 

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.060
from the deeper parts of the lesion.

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:12.050
Clean and abrade the surface gently, but with determination. 

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:19.290
Collect in a capillary tube, with or without the aid of a suction bulb.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.210
[The physician holds up first a capillary tube, then a suction bulb as he describes the necessary steps.]

00:07:22.389 --> 00:07:26.989
The ends of the tube then seal by thrusting
into sterile petrolatum. 

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:33.000
The blank form filled out. 

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:39.860
And the capillary tube then returned to the container which is sealed and sent at once.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:49.099
Request report by phone or wire if positive.
In his eagerness to prove a case, let no physician

00:07:49.099 --> 00:07:54.979
be betrayed into doing either a provocative
procedure or a therapeutic test in a doubtful situation.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.600
If the patient will not wait, he should agree
to go ahead under such circumstances with

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:08.719
a full year or more of standard treatment
for syphilis regardless of the test results.

00:08:08.719 --> 00:08:14.530
If the first darkfield fails or is negative,
repeat at one or two-day intervals,

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:18.470
using salt-solution wet dressings or soaks between time.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.640
Persistence over a week, if possible, is essential.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:26.880
Examination of women patients for primary syphilis is rarely adequate. 

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:31.780
Lesions on the external genitalia are inconspicuous and symptomless.

00:08:31.789 --> 00:08:37.310
About 60 percent of chancres of the genitalia
in women occur on the cervix and require darkfield

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:44.039
on a specimen obtained with a long capillary
pipette, on speculum exposure of the cervix.

00:08:44.039 --> 00:08:50.480
The clinical appearances ranging from a vesicle
to a pseudo-carcinoma are totally deceiving.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:54.190
Make speculum examination of all exposed women.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:09:00.140
Most syphilis in women is not diagnosed until
secondaries appear, and often not then,

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:05.100
since the tendency is towards constitutional rather than eruptive manifestation.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:10.610
Watch for the extragenital primary lesions.
Be chronically suspicious of all slow-healing,

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:16.120
indolent, indurated lesions with associated
regional lymph adenopathy.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:23.120
Why is a physician's own primary infection
so rarely diagnosed before secondaries appear?

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:28.530
Not because he has no chancre, though this
may occur in needle-prick inoculations,

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:33.120
but because he has a low index of suspicion for the disease.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:38.530
Either he never suspects at all, or he gets
panicked and makes diagnosis impossible by

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:42.830
premature treatment. He rarely turns to the
darkfield. 

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.440
Seldom to the blood test until too late.

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:53.440
If the darkfield is reported repeatedly negative,
and the blood likewise is syphilis-excluded,

00:09:54.720 --> 00:10:01.260
not within the first three months, serologic
follow-up of blood tests every week after

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.830
the third week...

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:08.480
...monthly after the second month, dating
from the time the lesion was first seen,

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:13.300
is as necessary in the diagnosis of early syphilis as the initial darkfield.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:21.020
Early syphilis develops slowly, often inconspicuously. Must be followed along with tests.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:27.360
Serologic follow-up for syphilis should be performed in all cases of gonorrhea.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:31.930
And in many nonspecific urethritity developing
after sexual exposure. 

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:37.100
Piecemeal and incomplete examination defeats many diagnoses of early syphilis.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:43.330
Strip every patient at the first visit, and examine the skin and mucosae, as well as the suspected

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.690
chancre or the part complained of.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:51.700
Secondaries may be found to prove a primary,
or a primary to prove up secondary

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:56.290
Some lesions that look like chancres are merely relapses in older infections.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:11:00.110
The ensemble of the case may determine the
diagnosis and treatment

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.580
as much as the blood test alone.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:09.760
The diagnosis of secondary syphilis today
rests on the fact that a competent laboratory

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:15.030
gives little short of 100 percent positive
Wassermann and precipitation tests

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.520
on florid secondary syphilis.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:23.070
A repeatedly negative blood test practically
excludes secondary syphilis. 

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:28.340
The problem is, therefore, to get suspicion aroused to the point of an adequate examination, then to

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:33.960
then to take a blood test, and lastly to avoid the gross occasional mistake 

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:37.540
of calling a non-syphilitic eruption syphilitic.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:43.950
The constitutional symptoms of early syphilis
are seldom specific enough to arouse suspicion.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:48.120
Suspicion should therefore attain the automatic status of a blood test 

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:50.610
for the disease on every new patient.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:56.700
Chronic headache, chronic sore throat, bone pains, and localized tenderness, persistent

00:11:56.840 --> 00:12:01.720
persistent anemia and weight loss in young women, would achieve new significance.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:08.080
A general lymph node enlargement or a palpable
spleen may be a diagnostic landmark.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:13.000
Relapses and recurrences of early syphilis are common under insufficient treatment

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.040
with the arsenicals and mercury by mouth.

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:23.840
Mucosal and genital relapses are gravely infectious, inconspicuous, evanescent, and numerically important.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:28.020
Examine the mouth and genitalia where most
of them occur.

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:34.500
Have darkfields, for these patients may be
seronegative. Suspect moist spots, moist papule,

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:39.640
fissures, split papules. Suspect piles.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:46.640
Suspect all rings, especially about the genitalia,
all groups of darkish, firm, or fleshy papules.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.970
And take blood tests.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:57.520
If you will undress patients, use good light
and sharp eyes and suspect, eternally suspect.

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:02.490
With the laboratory at your elbow, you will
rarely miss early symptoms. 

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:05.580
But a moment's loss of vigilance may let it pass.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:25.730
[Fix?] or study the lesion, or part,
with one gloved hand. 

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:30.820
Tell the patient what you are aiming to do. Have him or her lie down.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:35.220
Do not use local anesthetics. 

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:41.640
Cautioning the
patient, rub the surface boldly with gauze.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:49.040
[The physician uses gauze to rub a patient's penis to obtain a fluid sample for testing.]

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:53.200
Scraping is rarely necessary unless dry or
crusted. 

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:59.560
Allow bleeding to subside spontaneously, and wipe off the clot.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:07.080
Gently squeeze the base of the lesion between thumb and forefinger,

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:13.540
tipping so as to collect the serum toward one side.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:17.180
[The physician demonstrates as he describes the procedure.]

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:23.600
Holding the capillary tube at a low angle
from the horizontal, allow capillarity

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:31.210
to draw the fluid into it. Or if a bulb is supplied, suck it in with very slight suction.

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:37.290
[The physician continues to draw the sample into the tube.]

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:46.320
Seal the ends of the tube with sterile petrolatum.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:59.730
If the lesion is dry despite manipulation,
proceed as follows: 

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:08.640
If an isolated part like penis or finger is involved, take hold of it, please, both hands.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:13.820
Throw a broad rubber band about it. In a number of turns, 

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:17.760
making congestive but not extreme pressure.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:26.340
[The patient's penis is wrapped in gauze and a rubber band.]

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:38.980
Protect with gauze wrapping first. Wait five
to 15 minutes. Use the suction bulb.

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:45.880
[The physician demonstrates the technique as he speaks.]

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:50.580
Or rig and use the sucker....

00:15:51.740 --> 00:16:01.540
applying the mouth of the smaller syringe to the lesion while you aspirate with the larger.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:13.500
Usually an abundance of serum is obtainable one way or the other. 

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:20.160
Aspiration of base or nodes requires experience.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:25.900
Of course, sterilize all infected materials.

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:32.300
Gonorrhea masks the onset of perhaps 15 to 20 percent of syphilis in males.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:37.240
The late discharge of a gonorrhea, or of a
nonspecific urethritis, 

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:41.040
should be examined for spriochetes more frequently than it is.

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:44.340
Smears are not satisfactory for such work.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:51.120
Immediately the specimen for darkfield examination is obtained. Draw blood for serologic tests for syphilis.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:58.680
Always use the two procedures parallel. Too often this is forgotten even in the best clinics in the world.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:04.100
The older the suspected lesion,
the more apt it is to be darkfield negative.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.340
The more probably seropositive the patient.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:24.500
This demonstrates the simple method of examining the anal-genital region in women

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:29.560
for infectious lesions, that which can be used in ordinary office practice.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:34.510
The patient lies on her right side on the
table under a divided sheet. 

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:40.780
The nurse raises the left knee and carries it well up onto the abdomen 

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:45.480
so that the patient assumes a modified Sims position.

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:50.630
The buttocks are then separated and you can see how complete is 

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:55.580
the exposure of the external genitalia and the anal region.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:14.280
Secondary syphilis is usually hard, not easy, to see. Use good light. 

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:18.760
Expect faint macules.  And papules.

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:24.580
Groups of follicular lesions, rather than
pustules, rings, and sores. 

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:30.300
A fleshy field of papules is suspicious.

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:39.690
Patchy hair and eyebrows warrant Wassermann.

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:48.820
Peer into the corners. Especially never forget the lips.

00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:55.710
[Dr. Stokes to patient:] Stick your tongue out. Put it over to the right. 

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:58.880
Over to the left. Out of your mouth.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:03.660
Way out. Go like that. Say "ahhhh."

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.720
[Male patient:] Ahhhh.

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:09.160
[Dr. Stokes:] Close your mouth.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:14.840
The anus and genitalia. Drop your trousers to your knees.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:22.040
Especially the foreskin...

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:28.940
the anterior surface of the scrotum.

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:41.340
Turn around. Stoop forward. The posterior
surface of the scrotum. The anus. 

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:50.510
Stand up. Turn back. The labia and perineum in women.

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:57.930
The palms and soles may show flat papules
which give the whole case away. 

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:01.260
The darkfield is useful in secondary syphilis.

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:05.920
Obtain specimens for it as with chancre, even
by scraping dry papules. 

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:11.360
Use it for the serologic tests. Make up the ensemble of a completely established case.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:20.690
Always look for the chancre and its [inaudible] when examining for secondary syphilis. 

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:23.380
Finding it often makes the case complete.

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:25.570
[Audience clapping]

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:30.980
[Narrator:] This treatment of syphilis is
presented by Dr. Harold N. Cole, 

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:33.420
of Western Reserve University in Cleveland. 

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:39.900
Dr. Cole is a member of the Council on Pharmacy and Chemistry of the American Medical Association.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:44.300
[Dr. Cole:] Fournier advised treating syphilis by alternating courses of mercury 

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:51.360
and purposeful rest periods over a term of three to four years, the so-called intermittent treatment.

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:57.820
The courses of treatment were shortened, and the rest periods were lengthened, as time went on.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:02.840
He claimed this mode of treatment
was necessary, as mercury is too toxic a drug

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:05.380
to be used continuously.

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:09.990
Limit your selection of drugs to preparations
accepted by the Council on Pharmacy and Chemistry

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:12.140
of the American Medical Association.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:17.460
The perfect anti-syphilitic drug should destroy
all the organisms of the disease in the body

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:23.210
without attendant harm to the host. Unfortunately,
no such drug exists.

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:27.770
Certain salts of arsenic and of bismuth best
answer these requirements. 

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:33.800
If it were possible to give syphilitic patients large enough doses of arsenicals and bismuth to cure them

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:38.270
in one course of treatment, there would be no necessity for planned treatment.

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:44.270
Human syphilis cannot be overwhelmed at one
fell swoop. It is a chronic disease in which

00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:47.350
the organisms only gradually disappear.

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:53.050
Larson claimed that the disease is merely
arrested. That the spirochetes never disappear.

00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:56.610
Such being the case, the fallacious argument of Fournier 

00:21:56.720 --> 00:22:01.140
for the intermittent treatment of syphilis is exposed.

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:08.040
In the rest periods, the organisms start to
multiply. Investigations have shown that a

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:13.820
continuous, rather than an intermittent type
of therapy, is preferable in early syphilis.

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:21.860
The spirochetes have no opportunity to increase
in numbers. Instead of purposeful rest periods,

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:25.250
following a course of arsenical injections,

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:31.559
this is followed, at once, by a further course
of bismuth treatment, and this in turn,

00:22:31.559 --> 00:22:35.200
by further arsenical therapy, and so on.

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:42.940
To illustrate the point, each circle indicates
an intravenous arsenical. 

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:46.060
[Lecturer begins drawing on chalkboard.]

00:22:46.220 --> 00:22:53.220
Each cross, an insoluble bismuth, given intramuscularly once a week.

00:22:55.180 --> 00:23:01.600
Indeed, the injections may overlap so that
there is actually continuous therapy.

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:06.760
The first bismuth injection being given with the last arsenical treatment and vice versa.

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:15.600
Thus... [doctor writes on chalkboard]

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:22.820
note the overlap of the drugs. Generally
the arsenical treatments are given in courses of ten.

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:28.300
The bismuth injections of six, eight
and later, ten or twelve.

00:23:28.460 --> 00:23:34.020
Often the first three arsenical treatments
in acute syphilis are given in a period

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:41.020
of one week, this in the hope of overcoming the acute infectious lesions of the disease.

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:46.800
Reactions are occasionally encountered from
these preparations used to combat syphilis.

00:23:47.660 --> 00:23:52.980
With bismuth and with mercury, the urine should
be examined weekly,

00:23:53.120 --> 00:23:59.040
and the teeth watched for evidence of stomatitis and a bismuth line.

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:05.240
Rarely with bismuth therapy are severe reactions noted. With arsenic on the other hand, 

00:24:05.620 --> 00:24:09.300
gastrointestinal upsets are not uncommon.

00:24:09.309 --> 00:24:13.649
And cutaneous disturbances from a fleeting
erythema or urticaria,

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:17.980
to a generalized exfoliation may be seen.

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:23.290
Hemorrhagic reactions are a signal for immediate discontinuance of further therapy. 

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:27.760
[Inaudible] likewise calls for great caution.

00:24:27.770 --> 00:24:34.390
In fact, any untoward reaction demands careful questioning and examination before further treatment.

00:24:35.720 --> 00:24:41.440
It is much easier to prevent reactions
than to treat them afterwards.

00:24:41.450 --> 00:24:50.240
In treating an acute syphilis, the earliest
possible diagnosis and administration of therapy

00:24:50.240 --> 00:24:57.240
are the goals. Know a few efficient anti-syphilitic
remedies and know them well.

00:24:57.440 --> 00:25:03.280
Arsphenamine is rarely employed outside of hospital and clinic practice. 

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:11.400
In administering the arsenicals, all apparatus must be carefully sterilized and cooled.

00:25:11.400 --> 00:25:16.740
[Doctor demonstrates handling of equipment.]

00:25:16.780 --> 00:25:24.900
Neo-arsphenamine is administered through carefully
pouring the contents of the glass containers

00:25:24.980 --> 00:25:28.840
previously floated in alcohol to ensure freedom from cracks.

00:25:28.900 --> 00:25:35.060
Over the surface apply to 8ccs of sterile
distilled water. 

00:25:36.220 --> 00:25:40.980
Gently rotate the container to ensure solutions.

00:25:42.950 --> 00:25:49.950
Draw up the contents in a 10cc syringe, using
a one and one-half inch fine needle.

00:25:50.560 --> 00:25:56.380
Introduce the needle through the skin parallel to and alongside the vein at the fold of the arm,

00:25:56.390 --> 00:25:59.020
using a tourniquet to swell up the vein.

00:25:59.020 --> 00:26:02.620
Then gently push the needle point well into
the vein, not through it. 

00:26:02.740 --> 00:26:07.660
Never inject the drug until sure, through aspiration and backflow of blood,

00:26:07.660 --> 00:26:11.920
that the entire needle aperture is in the vessel.

00:26:12.300 --> 00:26:20.300
After removing the tourniquet, then slowly
inject the drug, employing at least two minutes.

00:26:21.360 --> 00:26:26.070
If the drug does not flow in smoothly and
easily, or if a swelling appears at the site

00:26:26.070 --> 00:26:32.650
of injection, the needle point is outside
the vessel wall and requires further manipulation

00:26:32.650 --> 00:26:34.250
or complete withdrawal.

00:26:34.250 --> 00:26:39.870
Be sure the needlepoint is free in the vessel. Moreover, be careful that the opening is not

00:26:39.870 --> 00:26:44.630
is not pressed against the vessel wall obstructing the easy flow. 

00:26:44.880 --> 00:26:49.920
Now we will repeat the action in slow motion and animation.

00:26:54.180 --> 00:27:04.740
[Animated image of skin showing subcutaneous tissue, fat, and vein.]

00:27:04.740 --> 00:27:15.060
[Animated image of point of needle piercing the skin  and subcutaneous layer, then entering the vein.]

00:27:19.280 --> 00:27:25.200
[Live action of procedure as doctor manipulates needle.]

00:27:25.200 --> 00:27:28.640
[Animated image of needle being withdrawn from vein.]

00:27:28.840 --> 00:27:46.000
[Image alternates between live action as doctor releases tourniquet and animated sequence of solution flowing through vein.]

00:27:51.440 --> 00:28:05.160
[Animated images of needle puncturing vein, partially puncturing vein, and infiltration of subcutaneous tissue.]

00:28:06.880 --> 00:28:11.800
If mapharsen is employed, it should be thoroughly aerated after being dissolved 

00:28:11.880 --> 00:28:16.500
to draw it up into the syringe  and forcibly expelling into the beaker.

00:28:16.640 --> 00:28:22.300
Mapharsen, in contra-distinction to the other arsenicals, should be rapidly injected.

00:28:23.560 --> 00:28:28.620
Bismuth injections are given by the intramuscular route only.

00:28:28.880 --> 00:28:34.960
The injections are given in the inner angle of the upper and outer quadrants of the buttocks.

00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:47.360
Employing a syringe with a one and one half inch needle, gauge 21 or 22, the drug has been

00:28:47.360 --> 00:28:50.840
drawn up from its container after careful
shaking. 

00:28:51.060 --> 00:28:54.480
Now sterilize the site with cotton and alcohol.

00:28:54.660 --> 00:28:59.240
Holding the syringe with needle attached like a pen...with a slight movement of the wrist

00:28:59.250 --> 00:29:05.020
backwards and forwards, the needle is boldly plunged deeply into the muscles.

00:29:05.020 --> 00:29:09.540
Then aspirate with the piston of the syringe
several times to be sure that the needle is

00:29:09.540 --> 00:29:14.760
not in a blood vessel. Holding the needle
base firmly with a free hand, the contents

00:29:14.760 --> 00:29:19.520
are then slowly injected into the muscle,
and the needle quickly withdrawn.

00:29:21.340 --> 00:29:26.520
A good bismuth preparation, where rapid action
is not essential, though prolonged in character,

00:29:26.740 --> 00:29:31.480
is an oil suspension of the bismuth subsalicylate, 12 hundredths of a gram, 

00:29:31.660 --> 00:29:36.140
two grains, metallic bismuth administered weekly.

00:29:36.150 --> 00:29:40.870
With bismuth salts dissolved in water or in
ethylene glycol, the injections should be

00:29:40.870 --> 00:29:47.870
given two or three times a week to keep the
therapeutic level at its proper height.

00:29:48.320 --> 00:29:55.040
To illustrate, in seronegative primary syphilis, give neo-arsphenamine, three-tenths of a gram.

00:29:56.460 --> 00:30:03.660
Repeat in three days. And three days
later with 45 hundredths to six-tenths of a gram.

00:30:04.380 --> 00:30:10.429
For the first three weeks, a bismuth injection
should be given once a week with the added

00:30:10.429 --> 00:30:13.369
hope of overcoming acute infectious symptoms.

00:30:13.580 --> 00:30:16.851
Thereafter, only between courses of therapy.

00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:19.480
Thus...

00:30:19.480 --> 00:30:30.980
[Doctor writes figures on the chalkboard.]

00:30:37.340 --> 00:30:41.260
Ten more arsenicals...

00:30:43.380 --> 00:30:47.140
and ten more bismuth injections.

00:30:49.480 --> 00:30:55.160
A Wassermann test is taken at the end of each course of arsenical therapy, 

00:30:55.300 --> 00:31:01.179
and one day after, and five days after the first injection of each succeeding course.

00:31:01.179 --> 00:31:07.559
The so-called provocative Wassermann reaction. A Wassermann reversal which persists negative

00:31:07.559 --> 00:31:13.690
has some significance; however syphilologists are more and more, emphasizing the necessity

00:31:13.690 --> 00:31:17.549
of a certain amount of treatment despite a
negative test.

00:31:17.549 --> 00:31:21.929
Potassium iodide may be used along with the
heavy metal injections. 

00:31:22.120 --> 00:31:26.080
A lumbar puncture should be performed early in the course of syphilis 

00:31:26.140 --> 00:31:29.160
to rule out central nervous system involvement.

00:31:29.160 --> 00:31:35.500
With seropositive primary and secondary syphilis,
a further course of arsenical injections and

00:31:35.500 --> 00:31:41.180
bismuth treatments are in order, thus aggregating a total of 40 of each 

00:31:41.180 --> 00:31:44.920
given in a continuous manner.

00:31:44.920 --> 00:31:50.340
In certain contigencies, it may be necessary to employ mercury instead of bismuth.

00:31:50.660 --> 00:31:55.340
An excellent substitute would be 80 injections of four grams each 

00:31:55.440 --> 00:32:00.320
of [inaudible] hydrogent 40R rubbed in, 30 minutes, by the clock.

00:32:00.330 --> 00:32:05.350
If all signs and symptoms of the disease have
disappeared at the end of one year, the patient

00:32:05.350 --> 00:32:09.919
may be put on probation and Wassermann tests
taken every two months.

00:32:09.919 --> 00:32:14.179
At the end of two and a half years there should
be general checkup, lumbar puncture, 

00:32:14.240 --> 00:32:16.880
and examination of cardiovascular apparatus.

00:32:17.520 --> 00:32:21.860
Thereafter, Wassermann tests and physical
examination every six months.

00:32:21.980 --> 00:32:27.820
At the end of five years, a Wassermann test and physical examination once a year suffices.

00:32:27.900 --> 00:32:33.360
Cooperative clinical studies have shown a
greatly lessened incidence of relapse since

00:32:33.360 --> 00:32:38.720
the institution of continuous therapy. The
infectious, moist papules of the lips and

00:32:38.840 --> 00:32:45.280
genitalia, the paraplegias, the ocular-motor
paralyses, are not seen so often.

00:32:45.290 --> 00:32:51.420
Moreover, the frequency of the Wassermann relapse seen early in the course of syphilis

00:32:51.420 --> 00:32:53.220
has dropped enormously.

00:32:53.230 --> 00:32:59.600
Relapse, that bugaboo of the physician, coming early in the course of syphilis, 85 percent

00:32:59.600 --> 00:33:04.090
of them intervening before the end of the
second year of the disease.

00:33:04.090 --> 00:33:10.930
Many of them infectious in character; for
example, a moist papule of the lip and of the genitalia.

00:33:12.200 --> 00:33:16.440
Intermittent, irregular treatment predisposes to relapse.

00:33:16.760 --> 00:33:23.220
Voluntary discontinuance of treatment and
inadequate treatment likewise contribute to

00:33:23.220 --> 00:33:30.210
the frequency of this symptom. Many more relapses
will be seen where the patient receives less

00:33:30.210 --> 00:33:34.040
than 20 injections of arsenical and of a bismuth
preparation.

00:33:34.040 --> 00:33:40.850
In fact, every case of acute syphilis should
receive at least 33 to 40 injections of an

00:33:40.850 --> 00:33:45.450
arsenical and of a bismuth preparation given
in such a manner that the patient 

00:33:45.580 --> 00:33:48.680
is continuously under therapy.

00:33:48.690 --> 00:33:53.830
In conclusion, in acute syphilis, make the
earliest possible diagnosis, 

00:33:53.880 --> 00:33:56.720
and institute treatment at once.

00:33:57.420 --> 00:34:04.500
Check all contexts and sources. Employ only tried and accepted drugs.

00:34:04.700 --> 00:34:11.060
Follow continuous therapy, of alternating courses of bismuth and of arsenicals.

00:34:11.920 --> 00:34:20.400
In a seronegative primary syphilis, use at least 30 injections of an arsenical and of a bismuth preparation, 

00:34:20.400 --> 00:34:25.240
 given in such a manner, that the patient is under continuous therapy.

00:34:25.240 --> 00:34:30.740
With secondary syphilis, give at least 40
injections of each. 

00:34:31.020 --> 00:34:35.720
Eternal vigilance is the price of the syphilis problem.

00:34:38.940 --> 00:34:44.240
[Narrator:] Dr. Paul A. O'Leary, Professor
of Dermatology and Syphilology in the

00:34:44.400 --> 00:34:50.020
Graduate School of Medicine of the University of Minnesota at Rochester, Minnesota. 

00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:52.819
He discusses latent syphilis.

00:34:54.120 --> 00:34:58.920
[Dr. O'Leary:] In latent syphilis, there are
no clinical signs or symptoms.

00:34:58.920 --> 00:35:05.220
Latency may develop spontaneously by the fourth year of the disease, or it may be produced earlier

00:35:05.220 --> 00:35:08.479
in the course by energetic treatment.

00:35:09.840 --> 00:35:14.880
It is during this phase of the disease that
it is possible to determine whether or not

00:35:14.880 --> 00:35:20.150
the patient is developing a defense mechanism against his infection or is lacking in this respect.

00:35:21.420 --> 00:35:27.299
Latency may be a temporary or a permanent
state. When temporary, the patient is in the

00:35:27.299 --> 00:35:31.390
process of developing aortitis, or changes,
in his central nervous system.

00:35:31.390 --> 00:35:32.380
[X-ray image shows an enlarged heart.]

00:35:32.380 --> 00:35:38.309
A patient who develops a permanent state of
latency is fortunate. When cure is not obtained

00:35:38.309 --> 00:35:42.900
in early syphilis, we endeavor then to produce
a permanent state of latency.

00:35:44.020 --> 00:35:50.319
Diagnosis of latent syphilis can be made only
after a complete physical examination has

00:35:50.319 --> 00:35:53.299
eliminated all evidence of cardiovascular
involvement.

00:35:53.299 --> 00:35:59.239
In addition, it is essential that the evidence
of syphilis be lacking in other viscera and

00:35:59.239 --> 00:36:03.999
the nervous system, and that the examination
of the spinal fluid be completely negative.

00:36:04.580 --> 00:36:09.520
If the examination reveals even presumptive evidence of an involvement of the heart,

00:36:09.529 --> 00:36:15.069
or the viscera, or the central nervous system, of course the diagnosis of latency is then discarded.

00:36:15.559 --> 00:36:23.059
If the x-ray of the chest shows evidence of
early aortitis, as is manifested in this plate,

00:36:23.489 --> 00:36:28.609
of course the diagnosis of latency is discarded and cardiovascular disease is substituted.

00:36:30.260 --> 00:36:35.600
The Wassermann or flocculation tests in latent
syphilis, may be either negative or positive.

00:36:36.630 --> 00:36:40.200
The treatment of latent syphilis cannot be
standardized.

00:36:40.740 --> 00:36:44.680
Indications for treatment, however, vary according
to various factors, 

00:36:44.920 --> 00:36:50.820
such as the age of the patient, the duration of the syphilis, the amount of previous treatment, 

00:36:51.080 --> 00:36:54.539
and the sex of the individual.

00:36:54.539 --> 00:37:01.319
If the disease has been present for 20 years or more, and there are no clinical signs or symptoms,

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:06.059
and the patient presents only a positive Wassermann test, the likelihood is

00:37:06.059 --> 00:37:09.200
that he is in a permanent state of latency.

00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:14.789
If a young woman in whom the period of latency
is not known, because of the fact that the

00:37:14.789 --> 00:37:18.549
early manifestations of the disease were not recognized,

00:37:18.549 --> 00:37:22.920
 it probably is advisable to treat such a patient.

00:37:22.920 --> 00:37:29.920
A few case examples will illustrate the variation
in the indication for the treatment of latency.

00:37:29.930 --> 00:37:36.190
A 62-year-old farmer has had syphilis for
40 years and had received treatment with pills

00:37:36.190 --> 00:37:39.430
when the secondary syphilis was recognized.

00:37:39.500 --> 00:37:43.100
He's had no treatment since, and is free from symptoms of syphilis.

00:37:43.340 --> 00:37:49.520
Flocculation tests of the blood are strongly
positive. In this type, treatment is not indicated.

00:37:49.529 --> 00:37:53.900
The patient is not infectious, and he has
controlled the disease for 40 years.

00:37:53.900 --> 00:37:58.880
He should be told that the syphilis may be
ignored, except that he report once a year

00:37:58.880 --> 00:38:05.049
for re-examination. A positive blood test
may also be ignored. Nothing is to be gained

00:38:05.049 --> 00:38:08.009
by repeating this test at subsequent visits.

00:38:10.500 --> 00:38:16.580
A man, 41 years old, has had syphilis for
12 years. He had a small amount of treatment

00:38:16.580 --> 00:38:21.780
at the time of the chancre, and a secondary
infection, and now has only a positive blood

00:38:21.789 --> 00:38:23.769
test as evidence of his having syphilis.

00:38:24.720 --> 00:38:30.140
His spinal fluid test is negative, and he
has no signs of cardiovascular syphilis.

00:38:30.600 --> 00:38:35.020
Treat this patient, giving him several courses of arsphenamine, and at least six courses of

00:38:35.029 --> 00:38:37.710
bismuth, 12 injections to the course.

00:38:37.710 --> 00:38:43.640
During the treatment period, re-examine him
for signs of cardiovascular syphilis.

00:38:45.740 --> 00:38:50.640
A young married woman of 33 does not know
when she acquired the disease. 

00:38:50.720 --> 00:38:56.579
The blood tests are positive, the spinal fluid is negative and no signs of visceral syphilis are present.

00:38:57.040 --> 00:39:01.720
She is anxious to have a child, and should
be intensively and energetically treated.

00:39:02.420 --> 00:39:07.519
She should have at least four courses of arsphenamine, six courses of bismuth.

00:39:08.380 --> 00:39:13.779
A woman with latent syphilis may give birth
to a syphilitic child even though she has

00:39:13.779 --> 00:39:19.210
been well-treated for the disease before she
became pregnant.

00:39:19.210 --> 00:39:23.670
Liberal use of bismuth in the treatment of
latent syphilis has resulted in the reversal

00:39:23.670 --> 00:39:29.090
of the Wassermann to negative in the great
majority. In fact, in 85 percent of these patients,

00:39:29.140 --> 00:39:32.740
when treated and observed for a
period of 10 years,

00:39:32.740 --> 00:39:37.700
the persistently positive Wassermann test,
or so-called Wassermann-Fast, is not a diagnosis.

00:39:37.700 --> 00:39:41.069
It's merely an accumulation of serological
reports.

00:39:41.560 --> 00:39:46.960
The persistently positive Wassermann has different
significance, not only in various patients,

00:39:46.960 --> 00:39:50.729
but also in various manifestations of syphilis.

00:39:50.729 --> 00:39:57.729
In the patient who remains a positive Wassermann,
in spite of continued treatment, the treatment

00:39:58.120 --> 00:40:04.120
should be stopped until the patient can be
clinically scrutinized in an effort to explain

00:40:04.130 --> 00:40:06.190
the Wassermann-Fast.

00:40:06.190 --> 00:40:11.799
In early syphilis, the Wassermann test may
remain positive when treatment is given insufficiently,

00:40:11.799 --> 00:40:18.799
or when it is inadequate, or when the spinal fluid Wassermann remains positive.

00:40:19.430 --> 00:40:25.180
In latent syphilis the serologic tests may
be permanently positive. If the clinical signs

00:40:25.180 --> 00:40:31.749
of syphilis are not present, and if the spinal
fluid test is negative, the age of the patient,

00:40:31.749 --> 00:40:32.920
the duration of the syphilis,

00:40:32.920 --> 00:40:37.180
and the amount of previous treatment are the
factors that determine whether the positive

00:40:37.180 --> 00:40:39.219
Wassermann has any significance.

00:40:39.219 --> 00:40:46.219
The serologic tends to become negative spontaneously
in the majority of patients with latent syphilis.

00:40:46.579 --> 00:40:51.789
Before permitting a patient with this type
of syphilis to go untreated, impress on him

00:40:51.789 --> 00:40:57.049
the need for annual re-examination to make
certain the signs of visceral syphilis

00:40:57.049 --> 00:40:58.949
are not becoming manifest.

00:41:00.180 --> 00:41:05.539
Only by these repeated clinical examinations
is it possible to determine if the patient

00:41:05.539 --> 00:41:07.799
is developing a permanent state of latency.

00:41:08.740 --> 00:41:14.339
Accordingly, in a patient with latent syphilis
who appears to be Wassermann-Fast, it is advisable

00:41:14.339 --> 00:41:19.349
to give an adequate amount of treatment if
this treatment has not been given previously.

00:41:19.349 --> 00:41:24.589
The treatment should consist of at least 24
injections of an arsphenamine preparation

00:41:24.589 --> 00:41:27.009
and 48 injections of bismuth.

00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:32.019
If this amount of treatment has been given
and the patient is still greatly concerned

00:41:32.019 --> 00:41:36.779
because the serologic tests remain positive,
the subsequent treatment may be limited

00:41:36.779 --> 00:41:38.229
to bismuth therapy.

00:41:38.229 --> 00:41:44.609
Two courses of bismuth, 12 injections to the
course, may be given each year for three years.

00:41:44.900 --> 00:41:50.420
In late syphilis, permanently positive serological
tests have different significance.

00:41:51.380 --> 00:41:59.760
In cardiovascular disease, neurosyphilis,
in visceral syphilis, and a type of hepatitis

00:41:59.809 --> 00:42:06.039
or cirrhosis, and osteosyphilis, and
in the latent syphilitic lesions of the mucous

00:42:06.039 --> 00:42:12.200
membranes, the tests tend to remain permanently
positive.

00:42:12.200 --> 00:42:20.000
In such cases, it is advisable to not treat
solely with the idea of reverting a serological

00:42:20.019 --> 00:42:26.499
test to negative, but it is rather with the
idea of treating according to the symptomatology

00:42:26.499 --> 00:42:29.229
and to the response displayed.

00:42:29.229 --> 00:42:35.450
If a patient with syphilis who has been under
your care wishes to marry it is urged that

00:42:35.450 --> 00:42:38.569
you have him bring his fiancee to your office,

00:42:38.569 --> 00:42:43.299
so that you may discuss with her the fact
that he has had syphilis, that he has had

00:42:43.299 --> 00:42:49.559
adequate treatment, but that he should report
to you for re- examination once a year

00:42:49.559 --> 00:42:52.259
for at least several years to come.

00:42:52.720 --> 00:42:57.279
Miss Carlton, Frank has told me that he wants to marry you, but before he does there are

00:42:57.279 --> 00:43:00.999
certain things about him that I think you
should know that I would like to discuss with you.

00:43:02.240 --> 00:43:06.760
Physicians now believe that it's more advisable
to discuss such affairs before marriage rather

00:43:06.769 --> 00:43:08.909
than after in order to avoid future trouble.

00:43:08.980 --> 00:43:11.071
[Miss Carlton:] Yes, Doctor.

00:43:11.560 --> 00:43:15.940
[Dr. O'Leary:] Six years ago I started to
treat Frank for syphilis. 

00:43:16.240 --> 00:43:23.020
How he acquired the disease is of no importance now. The important point is that you should know the facts.

00:43:23.780 --> 00:43:26.960
[Miss Carlton:] But, Doctor, doesn't that
make our marriage impossible?

00:43:27.220 --> 00:43:32.540
[Dr. O'Leary:] No indeed. Here are the circumstances
of Frank's case. The patient with acute syphilis

00:43:33.080 --> 00:43:35.340
is adequately and thoroughly treated.

00:43:35.840 --> 00:43:40.420
And if the blood tests remain negative for
a period of five years after the treatment

00:43:40.430 --> 00:43:45.630
has been completed, he may marry without danger
of spreading the infection.

00:43:46.300 --> 00:43:51.880
The same is true of patients with latent syphilis.
If they undergo adequate treatment and have

00:43:51.880 --> 00:43:55.520
negative blood tests for a period of five
years following the treatment,

00:43:55.680 --> 00:43:58.880
 they likewise may marry without danger of infecting.

00:43:59.060 --> 00:44:04.160
Frank has had acute syphilis and has had good
treatment and observation.

00:44:04.240 --> 00:44:08.329
There are now no clinical signs of the disease and he may marry without danger to you.

00:44:09.660 --> 00:44:12.200
[Miss Carlton:] Oh, I thought that disease
could not be cured.

00:44:13.080 --> 00:44:16.580
[Dr. O'Leary:] Miss Carlton, Frank had the
good fortune to start treatment 

00:44:16.660 --> 00:44:21.060
at the beginning of his infection. He has been regular in his treatments,

00:44:21.060 --> 00:44:23.440
and I don't believe he has missed a single one.

00:44:23.450 --> 00:44:27.999
With the result that his tests have now been
negative for the past five years.

00:44:27.999 --> 00:44:30.559
In addition, his spinal fluid is likewise negative.

00:44:31.700 --> 00:44:36.720
All of these facts, [inaudible], taken together,
constitute what we today call the criteria

00:44:36.729 --> 00:44:43.079
for the cure of syphilis. Each year hereafter, if these tests remain negative, 

00:44:43.079 --> 00:44:45.559
the greater is the factor of cure.

00:44:45.559 --> 00:44:48.229
[Miss Carlton:] Is there no danger of my getting
syphilis from him?

00:44:48.229 --> 00:44:52.690
[Dr. O'Leary:] No, not now. Frank is past
the infectious period of the disease.

00:44:53.280 --> 00:44:56.600
[Miss Carlton:] Even so, I do not believe
we should have children.

00:44:56.600 --> 00:44:59.579
[Dr. O'Leary:] On the contrary, it will be
quite all right for you to have children.

00:44:59.579 --> 00:45:02.769
You know, syphilis is transmitted to the child
by the mother.

00:45:03.560 --> 00:45:08.779
So I'll ask but one thing of you, and one
of Frank. When you believe you are pregnant,

00:45:08.779 --> 00:45:13.279
I think you should come in immediately and
have a Wassermann test made.

00:45:13.279 --> 00:45:18.659
As to Frank, I'm anxious that he come back
once a year for a general examination. 

00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:23.339
Otherwise, I have nothing to offer you but my good wishes.

00:45:24.500 --> 00:45:30.520
[Narrator:] The treatment of syphilis in the
prospective mother is presented by Dr. James R. McCord, 

00:45:30.540 --> 00:45:34.880
Professor of Obstetrics and Gynecology
in Emory University School of Medicine, 

00:45:35.020 --> 00:45:37.360
Atlanta, Georgia.

00:45:37.760 --> 00:45:42.740
[Dr. McCord:] Syphilis, as a complication
of pregnancy, occurs frequently.

00:45:42.900 --> 00:45:49.140
The effect of syphilis upon pregnancy depends upon the activity of the disease in the mother.

00:45:49.140 --> 00:45:56.220
Syphilis may be recent and active, it may be moderately active, or it may be latent and inactive.

00:45:57.060 --> 00:46:01.760
If the disease is active, the baby will surely be syphilitic.

00:46:01.769 --> 00:46:08.680
If it is moderately active, the baby may be
syphilitic. Babies born apparently free of

00:46:08.680 --> 00:46:13.280
the disease of syphilitic mothers,
are born of those mothers 

00:46:13.280 --> 00:46:16.380
who have a latent and inactive syphilis.

00:46:16.920 --> 00:46:23.220
Babies born alive, of mothers with positive
Wassermann reactions, are hazardous risks.

00:46:23.579 --> 00:46:28.779
Only prolonged observation and repeated Wassermann
tests should convince one 

00:46:28.840 --> 00:46:32.559
that these babies are free of the disease.

00:46:32.559 --> 00:46:39.519
A well-done blood Wassermann test that is
strongly positive on a pregnant woman means syphilis.

00:46:39.960 --> 00:46:45.160
Pregnancy has no influence upon the reliability of this positive test.

00:46:45.160 --> 00:46:51.109
It cannot be too strongly emphasized that
the test be made by a competent laboratory,

00:46:51.109 --> 00:46:56.169
and not by incompetent technicians and doctors'
office laboratories.

00:46:56.940 --> 00:47:03.980
The positive blood Wassermann reaction is
the only means of making diagnosis of syphilis

00:47:04.080 --> 00:47:08.720
in the great majority of pregnant women who have the disease. 

00:47:08.820 --> 00:47:10.960
If in doubt, repeat the test.

00:47:11.160 --> 00:47:17.220
Certain treatment during pregnancy prevents
the disease in the baby in 95 percent of

00:47:17.229 --> 00:47:21.509
cases regardless of the activity of the disease in the mother.

00:47:21.509 --> 00:47:26.859
It is a generally accepted opinion that the
object of this treatment during pregnancy

00:47:26.859 --> 00:47:33.199
is to prevent syphilis in the baby. Make no
effort to cure the disease in the mother.

00:47:33.600 --> 00:47:40.180
Begin treatment immediately the diagnosis
is made. Treat weekly until labor begins.

00:47:40.190 --> 00:47:45.690
Repeat blood Wassermann tests are not necessary
and probably not desirable.

00:47:45.690 --> 00:47:51.270
Cessation of the treatment because of a negative
Wassermann reaction is inexcusable. 

00:47:51.640 --> 00:47:57.180
Ten consecutive weekly treatments are effective in the very large majority of pregnancies.

00:47:57.320 --> 00:48:03.459
However, make every effort to begin the treatment before the fifth month of pregnancy.

00:48:03.459 --> 00:48:09.759
Arsenic is a drug of greatest value. Shall arsphenamine
or neo-arsphenamine be given?

00:48:10.140 --> 00:48:15.959
Use the one with which you are the more familiar and can the better administer.

00:48:15.959 --> 00:48:21.679
The commandment is use arsenic in small doses,
constantly and continuously. 

00:48:22.080 --> 00:48:25.660
Give with the stomach empty and after a mild laxative.

00:48:25.670 --> 00:48:28.130
Take the blood pressure. 

00:48:30.880 --> 00:48:33.720
Examine the urine for [inaudible]. 

00:48:34.680 --> 00:48:39.239
Question the patient carefully about any sort of reaction from the last dose.

00:48:39.840 --> 00:48:46.240
If in doubt, play safe. Omit the arsenic for
a time. The arsenic must be given slowly.

00:48:46.869 --> 00:48:53.390
No preparation of the patient. Rapid injection
in large doses often leads to trouble.

00:48:53.390 --> 00:48:59.279
Unfortunately treatment is not begun with
a majority of pregnant women until after the

00:48:59.279 --> 00:49:04.379
fifth month of pregnancy. Because of this,
we prefer the concurrent use 

00:49:04.380 --> 00:49:06.299
of arsenic and a heavy metal.

00:49:06.299 --> 00:49:11.799
A dose of arsenic, neo-arsphenamine in our clinic, is 45-hundredths of a gram. 

00:49:12.300 --> 00:49:18.380
Never more, very rarely less. Two mild mercurial inunctions are given weekly.

00:49:18.769 --> 00:49:23.069
We think that mercury is tolerated better
by pregnant women than bismuth. 

00:49:23.280 --> 00:49:28.420
It causes no discomfort, and is more apt to be continued without interruption. 

00:49:28.720 --> 00:49:32.580
Mercury has the additional advantage of being cheaper.

00:49:32.589 --> 00:49:40.169
We repeat, make every effort to begin treatment
early, during the first two months of pregnancy.

00:49:40.759 --> 00:49:45.519
If the treatment is begun early, alternating
courses of arsenic and a heavy metal,

00:49:45.660 --> 00:49:49.440
preferably bismuth, may be given upon the best authority.

00:49:49.580 --> 00:49:53.900
Care should be exercised at the first and
last courses of the arsenic.

00:49:54.520 --> 00:49:58.960
Treat every syphlitic woman throughout each pregnancy without regard

00:49:59.060 --> 00:50:02.280
to the duration of the syphilis or to previous treatment.

00:50:02.289 --> 00:50:06.909
Pregnancy does not cause any more false positive reactions than occur among 

00:50:07.200 --> 00:50:14.940
the average non-syphilitic population. It does cause many false negative reactions.

00:50:16.080 --> 00:50:21.120
The benefits of present knowledge as to the
prevention of congenital syphilis can only

00:50:21.130 --> 00:50:26.490
be used to the full advantage when women are
universally taught the necessity 

00:50:26.680 --> 00:50:29.860
for early and continuous prenatal care.

00:50:29.869 --> 00:50:36.869
There can be no doubt but that almost the entire responsibility for safe teaching is ours.

00:50:37.320 --> 00:50:42.040
Syphilis is no respecter of person or social
standards. 

00:50:42.260 --> 00:50:47.700
Make an opportunity to get blood for a Wassermann on every pregnant woman.

00:50:48.000 --> 00:50:53.660
Treat those with positive reactions gently
and continuously. 

00:50:54.080 --> 00:50:58.720
The ideal of the medical profession is the saving of human life. 

00:50:58.740 --> 00:51:05.999
When, where, and how can it be more beautifully illustrated than in the prevention of congenital syphilis?

00:51:07.160 --> 00:51:12.680
[Narrator:] Congenital syphilis is the topic
of Dr. Philip C. Jeans, Professor of Pediatrics

00:51:12.680 --> 00:51:17.799
in the State University of Iowa College of
Medicine at Iowa City.

00:51:18.900 --> 00:51:24.420
[Dr. Jeans:] Syphilis in the child differs
from syphilis in the adult in only a few important ways.

00:51:25.700 --> 00:51:31.940
Such differences as occur are dependent
on differences in the host rather than in the spirochetes.

00:51:32.900 --> 00:51:39.090
The high mortality of infantile syphilis has
no counterpart in early syphilis of the adult.

00:51:40.190 --> 00:51:44.039
This is true also for the extensive bone changes.

00:51:45.360 --> 00:51:51.719
And the deeply infiltrating and scarring skin
lesions of the face found frequently in syphilitic infants.

00:51:51.769 --> 00:51:53.300
[Film of child's mouth being held open to
show crooked and missing teeth.]

00:51:53.300 --> 00:51:55.440
And the dystrophic changes in the teeth 

00:51:55.540 --> 00:52:00.200
sometimes observed in older children as a result of infantile syphilis.

00:52:01.860 --> 00:52:08.319
Keratitis is by far the most frequent lesion
of late congenital syphilis.

00:52:08.319 --> 00:52:11.999
But it is rare in acquired syphilis of the adult in whom it occurs 

00:52:12.100 --> 00:52:16.160
in the secondary stage of the disease.

00:52:16.400 --> 00:52:22.340
Congenital syphilis differs from acquired
syphilis also in that the infection is transmitted

00:52:22.349 --> 00:52:27.559
by way of the placenta to the infant, and
no primary lesion exists in the infant.

00:52:28.400 --> 00:52:34.120
Because of the absence of a primary lesion,
syphilis of the infant is often designated

00:52:34.130 --> 00:52:38.510
early or infantile syphilis instead of secondary syphilis.

00:52:38.600 --> 00:52:45.500
And for the same reason the tertiary stage is often called the late stage.

00:52:45.509 --> 00:52:51.369
The diagnosis of syphilis is made in the same manner in the child as in the adult. 

00:52:51.620 --> 00:52:59.220
Darkfield examination is useful when early skin lesions exist. Without interpretation, the Wassermann

00:52:59.329 --> 00:53:04.359
reaction is not reliable for diagnosis in
the first two months of life.

00:53:04.360 --> 00:53:09.180
A syphilitic baby may have a negative reaction at birth, and a non-syphilitic baby 

00:53:09.220 --> 00:53:16.980
of a syphilitic mother may have a positive reaction for a short time by passive transfer from the mother.

00:53:17.480 --> 00:53:23.100
By two months, or at most, three months of
age, these irregularities disappear,

00:53:23.780 --> 00:53:28.460
and a properly performed Wassermann reaction may be accepted as proof 

00:53:28.520 --> 00:53:31.900
of the presence or absence of syphilis.

00:53:32.359 --> 00:53:38.509
Throughout the remainder of childhood, a positive
reaction is obtained as long as any activity

00:53:38.509 --> 00:53:44.369
of the spirochetes exists. And a persistently
negative reaction may be accepted as

00:53:44.580 --> 00:53:52.640
good evidence of absence of the disease, or its cure, either spontaneously or as a result of treatment.

00:53:54.119 --> 00:54:00.479
The diagnosis of syphilis in the child cannot
be made by examination of the parents.

00:54:00.680 --> 00:54:08.100
Syphilitic parents may not have transmitted the infection. Or the examination may give negative results

00:54:08.109 --> 00:54:10.769
even though the child is syphilitic.

00:54:11.200 --> 00:54:17.760
Syphilis is to be diagnosed only by examination of the individual in question.

00:54:17.980 --> 00:54:24.839
The clinical signs of syphilis are valuable in diagnosis.
But as compared to the value of a properly

00:54:24.839 --> 00:54:30.349
performed Wassermann test, they are relatively unimportant.

00:54:30.349 --> 00:54:36.449
The diagnosis is incomplete in all instances
without the results of a Wassermann test.

00:54:36.800 --> 00:54:44.420
Blood for the test is obtained from an older child as easily and in the same manner as from an adult.

00:54:45.320 --> 00:54:51.580
Obtaining blood from an infant is easy when
the mental hazard of belief in its difficulty

00:54:51.589 --> 00:54:57.690
has been overcome. Usually some suitable vein
is found accessible.

00:54:57.690 --> 00:55:04.690
This may be at the elbow, wrist, or ankle,
or it may be in the scalp. 

00:55:05.880 --> 00:55:13.200
In the majority of infants, the external jugular vein is the one most readily available.

00:55:13.209 --> 00:55:20.079
This vein is brought into prominence by placing
the baby on its back, with the shoulders elevated

00:55:20.079 --> 00:55:27.079
on a pillow or sandbag, and the neck extended
and rotated.

00:55:29.949 --> 00:55:33.829
The crying of the baby when the skin is pricked
with the needle

00:55:34.000 --> 00:55:39.959
causes the vein to stand out firmly so that it is easily entered.

00:55:39.959 --> 00:55:45.869
The treatment of the infant and child with
syphilis depends on the same fundamental principles

00:55:45.869 --> 00:55:51.190
as at any other age, and the same general
plan of treatment is successful.

00:55:52.630 --> 00:55:56.290
In the case of the young infant with active
or florid syphilis, 

00:55:57.280 --> 00:55:59.520
it is necessary to start treatment cautiously.

00:56:00.460 --> 00:56:06.400
Starting treatment in such a baby with a full
dose of one of the arsphenamines would usually

00:56:06.400 --> 00:56:09.760
be a direct cause of its death. 

00:56:10.040 --> 00:56:14.040
It is preferable to get preliminary treatment with bismuth or mercury.

00:56:15.209 --> 00:56:20.999
This is to be followed by fractional and increasing
doses of arsphenamine until the full dose

00:56:20.999 --> 00:56:27.999
has been reached, after which time the regular
full dosage routine may be followed.

00:56:29.280 --> 00:56:34.640
For the arsphenamine treatment of syphilis
in infants and children, it is our own preference

00:56:34.650 --> 00:56:40.589
to use the intravenous route. For those who
prefer the intramuscular route, the choices

00:56:40.589 --> 00:56:46.150
among the arsphenamines is limited practically to sulpharsphenamine.

00:56:46.150 --> 00:56:52.790
Consequently, sulpharsphenamine has become popular in the treatment of syphilis in infants and children.

00:56:53.240 --> 00:56:58.220
Because dermatitis and other
reactions are more common with sulpharsphenamine

00:56:58.650 --> 00:57:05.529
than with old salvarsan, the latter drug administered by the intravenous route is to be preferred.

00:57:06.300 --> 00:57:12.520
A little practice makes intravenous therapy
relatively simple, even in the infant.

00:57:13.190 --> 00:57:19.559
Although congenital syphilis is reputed to
be most difficult or even impossible to cure,

00:57:19.559 --> 00:57:25.319
with few exceptions the disease is curable.
In the infant, cure is accomplished easily

00:57:25.580 --> 00:57:30.480
and often with only a few months of appropriate treatment.

00:57:30.670 --> 00:57:35.630
In the older child, the disease is more persistent, and in a few instances, 

00:57:36.300 --> 00:57:42.060
as much as seven or eight years of uninterrupted, systematic therapy is required. 

00:57:42.760 --> 00:57:47.600
In these cases, perseverance on on the part of the physician 

00:57:47.760 --> 00:57:52.200
and faithfulness of treatment on the part of the patient are essential.

00:57:55.660 --> 00:58:01.859
[Narrator:] Late manifestations and neurosyphilis
are presented by Dr. Joseph Earl Moore of

00:58:01.859 --> 00:58:06.069
John Hopkins University School of Medicine,
Baltimore.

00:58:07.160 --> 00:58:09.780
[Dr. Moore:] Syphilis of the central nervous
system is responsible 

00:58:09.900 --> 00:58:12.500
for as many deaths as cardiovascular syphilis.

00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:17.600
 It causes a far larger proportion of invalidism and incapacity.

00:58:17.609 --> 00:58:21.459
Syphilis of these two systems accounts for
at least 90 percent of the deaths from this infection.

00:58:22.190 --> 00:58:27.599
Though the nervous system is probably invaded by the organism in every infected person,

00:58:27.599 --> 00:58:31.779
only about 25 percent of them, if untreated
or badly treated, 

00:58:31.780 --> 00:58:35.940
will subsequently develop clinical evidences of neurosyphilis.

00:58:35.940 --> 00:58:41.289
The interval between infection and the development
of symptoms varies from a few weeks or months

00:58:41.289 --> 00:58:45.280
in the case of acute syphilitic meningitis,
to many years

00:58:45.280 --> 00:58:50.420
in the cases of late meningo-vascular neurosyphilis, tabes dorsalis, or paresis.

00:58:50.430 --> 00:58:55.599
This interval may be materially shortened
by the improper treatment of early syphilis.

00:58:55.599 --> 00:58:57.859
Remember the following simple facts:

00:58:57.859 --> 00:59:02.419
First, invasion of the nervous system may
be detected early in the course of the disease,

00:59:02.640 --> 00:59:05.640
usually years before the appearance of symptoms.

00:59:06.080 --> 00:59:08.800
This form of neurosyphilis, known as asymptomatic,

00:59:09.320 --> 00:59:12.680
 must be searched for in every patient, early or late,

00:59:13.060 --> 00:59:16.880
 by routine lumbar puncture and examination of the spinal fluid.

00:59:16.880 --> 00:59:20.140
Second, neurosyphilis is a great imitator.

00:59:20.340 --> 00:59:23.980
Acute syphilitic meningitis often mimics four other conditions. 

00:59:24.100 --> 00:59:27.040
For example, tuberculous-meningitis, and brain tumor.

00:59:27.749 --> 00:59:33.749
Late meningo-vascular neurosyphilis is easily confused with at least 17 other diseases.

00:59:33.749 --> 00:59:39.699
Disseminated sclerosis, Bell's palsy, migraine,
and cerebral arterial sclerosis are examples.

00:59:41.780 --> 00:59:48.020
Tabes dorsalis, usually so typical, may nevertheless
masquerade for years as one of 12 other fairly

00:59:48.040 --> 00:59:52.220
common conditions, including neuritis or rheumatism for lightning pains,

00:59:52.480 --> 00:59:57.640
 infected corns for perforating ulcer, or hypertrophic arthritis for Charcot's joint.

00:59:58.720 --> 01:00:02.020
Dementia paralytica is often recognized too
late 

01:00:02.500 --> 01:00:06.680
because the physician suspected instead one of 13 other conditions, 

01:00:06.940 --> 01:00:12.140
such as neurasthenia, psychoneurosis, hysteria, epilepsy, or chronic alcoholism.

01:00:19.560 --> 01:00:23.640
Remember that neurosyphilis may imitate or be imitated by many other diseases,

01:00:24.060 --> 01:00:25.640
medical or neurologic. 

01:00:26.520 --> 01:00:31.420
Use your flashlight to look for one of the commonest physical signs present in all types.

01:00:32.969 --> 01:00:37.589
The Argyll Robertson pupil in its early or
late stages. 

01:00:39.640 --> 01:00:44.980
And use your reflex hammer to look for the other, changes in the deep reflexes. 

01:00:48.060 --> 01:00:54.140
Employ a routine blood Wassermann test in every patient with any neurologic or psychiatric abnormality.

01:00:55.369 --> 01:00:59.249
When the blood Wassermann is positive or even if it is negative, when history and

01:00:59.249 --> 01:01:04.640
physical findings are highly suggestive, examine the cerebrospinal fluid.

01:01:04.640 --> 01:01:09.760
In taking spinal fluid for examination, the
patient is placed on his side 

01:01:09.920 --> 01:01:15.120
with his back to the operator. The skin is sterilized with iodine and alcohol.

01:01:15.349 --> 01:01:21.499
The shoulders are placed on a level with the
hips. The head is flexed as far as possible,

01:01:21.499 --> 01:01:26.660
and the knees drawn up on the thigh. The back should be in a straight line.

01:01:26.660 --> 01:01:31.089
Sterile towels are placed beneath the patient's side and on top over the patient's back.

01:01:31.900 --> 01:01:34.520
The operator thoroughly washes his hands.

01:01:34.860 --> 01:01:40.900
The use of sterile rubber gloves is not mandatory.
If the patient is nervous or highly excitable

01:01:41.599 --> 01:01:48.599
and can stand little pain, it is best to use
local anesthesia to avoid pain and struggling.

01:01:48.809 --> 01:01:52.429
The space between the second and third, third and fourth, 

01:01:52.620 --> 01:01:55.860
or fourth and fifth lumbar interspaces is utilized. 

01:01:56.080 --> 01:01:58.380
The widest space should be chosen.

01:01:58.390 --> 01:02:03.199
Since post-puncture headaches are due to fluid
leakage through the puncture wound of the

01:02:03.199 --> 01:02:09.180
dura, a fine needle, sharply pointed with
a well-fitting stillett should be used.

01:02:09.180 --> 01:02:14.529
The needle is inserted directly, or with a
slightly oblique tilt toward the head and inward.

01:02:15.620 --> 01:02:19.180
Resistance is met until the dura is pierced.

01:02:19.180 --> 01:02:25.089
The needle should not be pushed further inward as it may strike the opposite vertebral wall

01:02:25.089 --> 01:02:29.969
and either cause bleeding from an epidural
vein or become blocked.

01:02:30.040 --> 01:02:42.320
[The spinal tap procedure is demonstrated.]

01:02:42.380 --> 01:02:47.880
As the fluid comes from the needle, it should be collected in a suitable sterile tube,

01:02:47.960 --> 01:02:52.000
various samples being used for the necessary examination.

01:02:52.160 --> 01:03:45.000
[The tube is shown filling with spinal fluid
from the needle inserted into the spinal area.]

01:03:50.820 --> 01:03:55.799
After the needle is removed, the puncture
wound is covered with a sterile dressing.

01:03:56.480 --> 01:04:02.860
The patient may then rest under observation until the physician considers his condition satisfactory.

01:04:02.860 --> 01:04:09.880
[A gauze bandage is placed over the puncture area.]

01:04:15.670 --> 01:04:20.799
For prognosis and for successful treatment
we must know the type of neurosyphilis.

01:04:20.799 --> 01:04:24.739
The management and outcome of acute syphilitic meningitis differ from those of 

01:04:24.920 --> 01:04:31.200
late meningo-vascular neurosyphilis, and this in turn, from those of tabes dorsalis or paresis.

01:04:31.300 --> 01:04:40.780
[A man wearing a hat and using a cane walks slowly along a path through a garden or park.] 

01:04:41.299 --> 01:04:47.269
The decision as to type of neurosyphilis requires,
for the asymptomatic variety, expert knowledge

01:04:47.269 --> 01:04:51.930
of the interpretation of spinal fluid tests
and of the response of these tests to treatment.

01:04:54.480 --> 01:04:59.340
For the late forms of clinical neurosyphilis,
we must apply expert knowledge of the biology

01:04:59.380 --> 01:05:05.619
and course of syphilitic infection, and more
than average experience in neurology, psychiatry

01:05:05.619 --> 01:05:10.479
and ophthalmology, coupled with a wide general
medical training.

01:05:11.260 --> 01:05:17.459
This latter permits not only neurologic localization
of the disease process, but also an appreciation

01:05:17.459 --> 01:05:22.170
of the importance of syphilitic lesions or
other coexisting diseases outside the nervous system.

01:05:24.089 --> 01:05:27.289
The physician who attempts to treat neurosyphilis 

01:05:27.580 --> 01:05:31.620
without more exact information then this catch-basket diagnosis,

01:05:31.630 --> 01:05:36.839
and by the same routine standard procedure applicable to early or latent syphilis,

01:05:36.839 --> 01:05:42.869
will do his patients far less than justice, and
he may actually do much harm.

01:05:42.869 --> 01:05:48.769
How shall a physician choose the treatment
method appropriate for his particular patient?

01:05:48.769 --> 01:05:50.949
Shall he use an arsphenamine and bismuth,

01:05:51.320 --> 01:05:54.120
and if so which preparations, and in what dosage?

01:05:55.580 --> 01:06:01.119
Shall he employ Tryparsamide with its attendant risk of visual damage and perhaps blindness.

01:06:02.300 --> 01:06:05.420
If so, how and under what circumstances?

01:06:05.920 --> 01:06:10.540
The subdural treatment by the Swift-Ellis
technique, or some modification of it,

01:06:10.780 --> 01:06:15.600
still indicated, and if so, under what conditions?

01:06:15.609 --> 01:06:21.329
Shall fever therapy be employed and if so,
when and by which of the multitudinous methods?

01:06:21.329 --> 01:06:25.320
Shall it be tertian or quartan malaria,
foreign protein shock, 

01:06:25.320 --> 01:06:28.680
or electrically or mechanically-induced fever?

01:06:29.780 --> 01:06:33.920
Certain forms of neurosyphilis demand certain
forms of treatment;

01:06:33.960 --> 01:06:38.261
for example, dementia paralytica and fever, especially malaria.

01:06:39.300 --> 01:06:42.260
Certain broad principles apply to diagnosis
and treatment. 

01:06:43.440 --> 01:06:49.519
These are, first: Identify the type of neurosyphilis as accurately as possible

01:06:49.520 --> 01:06:53.579
by neurologic, psychiatric, and serologic examinations.

01:06:53.579 --> 01:06:57.719
Second, be familiar with the patient's general physical condition. 

01:06:58.200 --> 01:07:02.080
Has he cardiovascular syphilis or other complicating diseases?

01:07:03.140 --> 01:07:08.460
Third, be familiar with the possibilities
and dangers of, and the special indications for,

01:07:08.940 --> 01:07:15.300
various treatment methods, including
tryparsamide, subdural, and febrile therapy.

01:07:15.430 --> 01:07:22.430
Fourth, the aim of treatment is, in order
of desirability: symptomatic relief, clinical arrest

01:07:22.630 --> 01:07:29.410
with freedom from subsequent progression
or relapse, and least important, serologic normality.

01:07:30.029 --> 01:07:36.269
Fifth, proceed by a system of trial and error
and except for special indications,

01:07:36.640 --> 01:07:40.619
use least dangerous and drastic treatment methods first.

01:07:41.100 --> 01:07:47.620
Sixth, the age changes in treatment by clinical
progress first, next by serologic progress.

01:07:48.420 --> 01:07:52.380
Seven, give each method of treatment a trial of at least six months, 

01:07:52.800 --> 01:07:55.959
controlled by spinal fluid examination.

01:07:55.959 --> 01:08:02.920
Eight, treatment must be prolonged. The minimum
under any circumstances is two to three years.

01:08:02.920 --> 01:08:06.840
Nine, if spinal fluid changes are refractory
to treatment, 

01:08:07.120 --> 01:08:11.759
give serious consideration to fever therapy before probation.

01:08:11.759 --> 01:08:15.719
Ten, post-treatment observation must be rigidly controlled 

01:08:15.740 --> 01:08:19.860
by a lifetime of periodic physical and serologic re-examination. 

01:08:20.800 --> 01:08:27.160
Eleven, the neurosyphilitic patient has a disease which was once, if it is not now, infectious.

01:08:27.630 --> 01:08:34.540
Examine his family. There are too many patients
with, and too few experts in, neurosyphilis.

01:08:35.100 --> 01:08:38.900
For some patients, continued expert care is essential throughout.

01:08:39.620 --> 01:08:42.520
For others, a periodic consultant is called.

01:08:42.760 --> 01:08:47.820
First, diagnosis and the planning of treatment to be carried out by the family physician.

01:08:47.960 --> 01:08:53.100
Second, to check the results at six to 12 month intervals, and to re-plan future progress.

01:08:54.220 --> 01:08:59.400
Third, in the application of special treatment methods, such as induced fever

01:08:59.409 --> 01:09:04.880
which, like gallbladder surgery, the inexperienced physician should never risk unaided.

01:09:05.860 --> 01:09:09.680
[Narrator:] This production is a cooperative
venture of the United States Public Health Service

01:09:09.900 --> 01:09:12.260
and the American Medical Association.

01:09:12.500 --> 01:09:18.680
In charge of the campaign against syphilis for the United States Public Health service is Dr. R. A. van der Linden.

01:09:19.920 --> 01:09:24.799
[Dr. van der Linden:] Twice as many people as live in the nation's capital are infected

01:09:24.799 --> 01:09:30.099
with syphilis each year. The Public Health Service estimates that approximately 

01:09:30.140 --> 01:09:41.080
518,000 new patients with early syphilis each year seek treatment from physicians, clinics, and hospitals.

01:09:41.700 --> 01:09:48.859
According to the American Social Hygiene Association,
a second half million people seek treatment

01:09:48.859 --> 01:09:55.599
over drugstore counters, from quacks, or other
unauthorized sources. Many remain untreated.

01:09:56.820 --> 01:10:01.780
The control of syphilis is related to the
private practice of medicine 

01:10:01.980 --> 01:10:07.200
in a way which is unique in public health work.

01:10:07.210 --> 01:10:14.830
For any program to be successful, it is essential
that the physician and the health agency cooperate.

01:10:16.619 --> 01:10:21.899
The widespread prevalence of syphilis indicates that there is a grave need 

01:10:21.900 --> 01:10:25.860
for the coordination of the work of both groups.

01:10:26.199 --> 01:10:29.819
The physician who accepts for treatment a
patient with syphilis, 

01:10:29.920 --> 01:10:34.420
assumes a very definite public obligation.

01:10:34.429 --> 01:10:40.320
The practice of administering a few doses
of arsphenamine to a syphilitic patient unable

01:10:40.320 --> 01:10:44.550
to pay private fees for the prolonged course
of treatment,

01:10:44.550 --> 01:10:50.480
and of charging large fees which the patient is barely able to pay, later permitting him

01:10:50.480 --> 01:10:54.579
to lapse permanently from treatment, is no
less than criminal.

01:10:55.349 --> 01:11:00.969
Such inadequately treated patients frequently become public health problems 

01:11:01.040 --> 01:11:04.400
because of the development of infectious relapse 

01:11:04.680 --> 01:11:10.780
and the frequency with which the late, crippling manifestations of the disease develop.

01:11:11.920 --> 01:11:18.320
When you accept a patient with syphilis, you
should likewise accept the responsibility

01:11:18.320 --> 01:11:24.080
of assuring yourself that he completes the
treatment schedule. 

01:11:24.580 --> 01:11:30.700
He should be told in the beginning that if he fails to do so, he will be reported to the health authorities.

01:11:31.960 --> 01:11:37.360
As a physician, you would not fail to report
to the proper health officials 

01:11:37.480 --> 01:11:42.920
a case of smallpox who was not abiding by public health laws.

01:11:43.760 --> 01:11:49.440
Public opinion makes it absolutely necessary that you take this action.

01:11:50.160 --> 01:11:56.370
Early syphilis is just as important from a
public health standpoint as is smallpox,

01:11:56.680 --> 01:12:03.540
and more apt to kill. Your responsibility to the
health department in the control of syphilis

01:12:03.550 --> 01:12:08.469
is no less than with smallpox or any other
infectious disease.

01:12:09.300 --> 01:12:16.000
Opinions differ as to the character and content of morbidity report forms. 

01:12:16.360 --> 01:12:22.240
It is generally agreed that such forms should be simple and require that the physician provide 

01:12:22.380 --> 01:12:32.020
only essential information, such as the patient's age, sex, color, marital status, 

01:12:32.140 --> 01:12:38.440
diagnosis and stage of disease, and information as to the date of onset.

01:12:39.520 --> 01:12:44.460
Most health departments make optional a system of reporting 

01:12:44.480 --> 01:12:48.320
which does not require the identification of the patient.

01:12:48.820 --> 01:12:55.540
Every patient with early syphilis should be
questioned as to his sexual contact,

01:12:55.550 --> 01:13:00.350
and the possibility that syphilis may have been so spread. 

01:13:00.940 --> 01:13:08.400
Much can be accomplished by attempting to bring in these contacts on a voluntary basis. 

01:13:08.680 --> 01:13:16.080
Send a message to them by the patient, or
a letter by mail. If these simple methods

01:13:16.179 --> 01:13:23.150
fail to produce results, send your nurse or
request the health authorities to provide

01:13:23.150 --> 01:13:28.170
the services of a satisfactorily trained person.

01:13:28.170 --> 01:13:33.630
Use the same system of follow-up for the holding of patients under treatment. 

01:13:34.120 --> 01:13:39.300
In doing case-finding and case-holding work for the private physician,

01:13:39.300 --> 01:13:45.550
a public health nurse loaned by the health
department should act as the agent of the

01:13:45.550 --> 01:13:51.179
private physician and not as an official representative
of the health department.

01:13:51.880 --> 01:13:58.180
Remember, however, that compulsory methods may be employed to advantage, at times,

01:13:58.590 --> 01:14:03.910
in holding patients under treatment, whereas such methods are apt to fail 

01:14:04.100 --> 01:14:07.460
in the finding of new cases.

01:14:08.180 --> 01:14:15.020
The health department, likewise, has definite
obligations to the physician in private practice.

01:14:15.030 --> 01:14:19.630
Health departments should provide free diagnostic services to physicians, 

01:14:20.140 --> 01:14:25.320
should distribute, without charge, anti-syphilitic drugs to the private physicians

01:14:25.520 --> 01:14:29.660
 for the treatment of all patients with this disease,

01:14:29.670 --> 01:14:34.230
and should provide consultation service including roentgenologic 

01:14:34.260 --> 01:14:39.860
and other expensive laboratory examinations for indigent patients.

01:14:40.720 --> 01:14:46.239
Booklets and pamphlets should be provided
by the health department for the public

01:14:46.239 --> 01:14:50.929
and particularly for the patients of private physicians.

01:14:50.929 --> 01:14:55.820
The United States Public Health Service, the
American Society of Clinical Pathologists,

01:14:55.820 --> 01:15:02.150
and state departments of health are now cooperating fully in the development of a system

01:15:02.150 --> 01:15:09.150
which ensures the performance of reliable sero-diagnostic tests for syphilis.

01:15:09.199 --> 01:15:14.900
The assistance and cooperation, which the
American Medical Association has given to

01:15:14.900 --> 01:15:21.900
national agencies, is a most favorable indication that a successful program, acceptable to health

01:15:21.980 --> 01:15:29.639
offices and physicians alike, is being organized
throughout the United States.

01:15:29.639 --> 01:15:36.639
Many state medical societies have likewise
exhibited an active interest. The vast prevalence

01:15:36.929 --> 01:15:44.469
of syphilis at the present time will be regarded as a reflection upon the ability of the present-day

01:15:44.520 --> 01:15:51.560
physician and health officer if this problem
is neglected and the disease permitted to run rampant.

01:15:53.520 --> 01:15:58.480
[Narrator:] If the campaign against syphilis
is to succeed, the general practitioner into

01:15:58.489 --> 01:16:03.849
whose office will come the great majority
of patients with this disease, must be aware

01:16:03.849 --> 01:16:07.329
of modern methods of diagnosis and treatment.

01:16:07.400 --> 01:16:12.420
He must take most seriously his obligation
in relation to the control of syphilis

01:16:12.429 --> 01:16:14.409
as a public health problem.

01:16:14.409 --> 01:16:18.449
The United States Public Health Service and the American Medical Association 

01:16:18.640 --> 01:16:25.960
are ready at all times to give to the physician every aid that they can give in this work.

01:16:27.300 --> 01:16:57.160
[Music]

